      "id": "ig8jduu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Ocean Relief – Meaning"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The ocean floor is divided into four major relief divisions: Continental Shelf, Continental Slope, Deep Sea Plain (Abyssal Plain), and Oceanic Deeps/Trenches.",
        "Ocean temperature decreases with increasing depth, featuring a rapid drop in the Thermocline layer between 100 meters and 1000 meters depth.",
        "Salinity is defined as the total weight of dissolved salts in grams contained in one kilogram of seawater, expressed in parts per thousand (‰).",
        "Factors affecting surface ocean salinity include evaporation, precipitation, freshwater inflow from rivers, and surface wind currents.",
        "The Halocline is a distinct oceanic layer where salinity changes rapidly with depth."
      ],
      "id": "nnpd747"
    },
