    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Continental shelves are the world's richest fishing grounds (e.g., Grand Banks) and store vast petroleum and natural gas resources.",
        "Equatorial waters record lower surface salinity than tropical regions due to heavy daily convectional rainfall and high relative humidity.",
        "The Mariana Trench in the Pacific Ocean contains the deepest known point on Earth, the Challenger Deep.",
        "Isotherms in the Southern Hemisphere run nearly parallel to latitudes due to the vast expanse of ocean water."
      ],
      "id": "e0g1w7q"
